      "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses #61366.\n\n`format_model_inspection()` previously assumed every worker's `get_model()` returns a `torch.nn.Module` and immediately descended into `named_children()` traversal. Non-torch worker backends (e.g. alternative runtime backends) trigger an `AttributeError` on `LLM.__repr__` because their model handle lacks torch-specific attributes.\n\n## Change\n\nAdd an `isinstance(model, nn.Module)` guard at the top of `format_model_inspection()` and fall back to `repr(model)` for non-torch handles. The call sites (`Worker.get_model_inspection` and `LLM.__repr__`) already handle any string return value.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Static: syntax check passes (`ast.parse`).\n- The change is purely defensive: it widens the accepted input contract without altering the torch path.\n- No GPU environment was available to run vLLM's own test suite in this sandbox.\n\n## AI assistance\n\nThis PR was drafted with AI assistance. The human author reviewed every changed line.",
